WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-2019, you were here.

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were talking about
who should the nominee be.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.205
You were making the argument
that the nominee should be

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
somebody who would
excite the base.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:09.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got the sense --
I think we both agreed --

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
that maybe that wasn't
Joe Biden.

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:14.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think, looking back
you underestimated

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
how he would perform
as a candidate?

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:19.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know --
Mea culpa on my own part.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I underestimated him
certainly

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:23.323 size:78% position:39%
in so far as the kind
of campaign he ran.

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:25.358
-Right. Except, you know,
the first three primaries

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:28.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
and caucuses, Bernie won
the popular vote in all three.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.865 line:92%
Biden was fourth, fifth, sixth

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:35.168 size:84% position:42%
So it didn't look like
it was going to happen.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:38.304 line:92%
And even the party, um --

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:41.508
whatever you call the part
hacks that run the party -

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:44.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
they panicked
and changed the rules

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get Bloomberg on that stage
and in the campaign.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
Remember that?
They had collectively decided,

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:52.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, shoot,
Biden's not going to make it

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got to get Bloomberg
in here

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:56.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we got to change the rules
so he can debate."

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.958 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So I think that, yes --

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
Honestly, I think,
now looking back,

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think Biden
did the right thing.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was criticized
constantly by Trump

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
for being in the basement,
but that's exactly

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:09.669
where I think I would have been,
with "SportsCenter" on,

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:13.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
because Trump
was defeating himself.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
The more Biden
just let Trump talk,

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
the more that Biden just -
the more that Trump

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:23.116
just kept doing one
wackadoodle thing after another,

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:27.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
that -- that was going to
guarantee his defeat.

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:30.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they asked people
now in these last couple weeks

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:33.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
who voted for Biden,
"What's the number-one reaso

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.360 line:92%
why you voted for Biden?"

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
58% said, "Because
I wanted to defeat Trump.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.531 line:92%
I wanted to remove Trump."

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:41.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's still the number-one
reason that they wanted.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I honestly believe --
Maybe I'm wrong,

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:47.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I want to hang
onto some belief that Bide

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:49.576 line:92%
is going to seize this moment.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:51.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
happy birthday by the way.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:53.246 size:84% position:42% line:92%
He's 78 years old here.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:59.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he knows that he's in that
final quarter of his life.

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I think
when people get to that age,

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:06.192
they want to go out believin
they've done something profound,

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they've really made
a difference.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't want to go out
because you passed

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:13.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
a good tax bill or trade bil
or whatever.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want to go out
because you saved

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.669 line:92%
the people of the United States,

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:20.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
because women finally
were equal under the law,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.444
that the racism and the violence
against Black people

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
was going to somehow
come to an end,

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we were going to stop
this mass incarceration

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:31.784 size:75% position:38%
and all these things
that he has a chance

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:34.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be remembered
in the way we remember,

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:36.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
say, John F. Kennedy,
who was president

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:41.828
for two and a half, two an
three quarters years. That's it.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:44.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yet look
how he's remembered.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:47.000 line:92%
So Biden has that chance.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the people
want him to succeed.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.740 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I really believe that.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:54.941 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I do.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.309 line:92%
And there's so much to get done.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:59.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
All of us have to be
actively involved in this.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.047 line:92%
We have to get the Senate.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
We all have to do
whatever we can

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:05.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
to help out in Georgia
between now and January 5th.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.921
Everybody in Georgia, you've
got to get registered to vot

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:08.721 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
